WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.629
The shortest game in professional League
of Legends history is the story of a

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:07.420
charming outlaw, unrequited love, a
heartfelt memorial

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:10.960
(Casting)

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.280
and the bitter fury of a game developer scorned.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:27.540
Jeon "Apdo" Sang-gil was once revered as one
of the greatest League of Legends players in the world.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.470
He conquered solo queue taking the top

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.420
spots in both Korea and China all while
playing four positions at the same time.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.100
"The sick thing about Apdo is he can
play practically every single role in

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.540
the game and be good enough to get
accounts super high up in Challenger.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.480
Now that's not even the case for Faker."

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.540
But Apdo wasn't trying to go pro

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.860
Apdo was Elo boosting.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.580
Apdo would take your
money and boost your account all the way

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:56.460
to the highest reaches of solo queue, all
while maintaining his own fantastic record.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.327
Obviously, Riot didn't like that.

00:00:58.327 --> 00:01:00.250
Riot's generally not a fan of when

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.240
people mess with the competitive integrity
of their game, so whenever they gathered

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:08.740
up enough evidence of Apdo's Elo boosting
they'd ban him, but then Apdo would show

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.860
up on a new account and the chase would
start all over again.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:15.280
The money was good, but there wasn't any glory in it

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.260
Faker had just come off his rookie season World Championship win.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.810
Meanwhile, Apdo,
the king of Korean solo queue was

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:27.100
running and hiding from Riot. He wasn't
getting a chance to test his mettle on

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.899
stage against Korea's best. So Apdo
gathered up a few friends from solo

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:36.280
queue and formed Team Dark. Led by their
misfit hero they would compete in the

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:41.709
Pandora Champions Winter 2013 to 2014
qualifiers and if they made it they

00:01:41.709 --> 00:01:45.800
would give Apdo a chance to show that he 
had what it took to go toe-to-toe with

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.500
the best players in the world.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.700
(Casting)

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.080
But the day before the offline qualifiers, Riot banned

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.480
Apdo from playing in professional
tournaments for two years, and banned his

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.980
main account for 1,000 years.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.400
That's not a joke. He's literally banned from

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.760
playing League of Legends until the year
3013.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:11.530
Allegedly this had to do with a girl who came to
Apdo for Elo boosting, but when she

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:16.080
developed feelings for him he turned her
down and she turned him in.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.920
Team Dark was forced to play without Apdo, and though
they made it into Champions, it just

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.780
didn't seem like their hearts were in it
anymore.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:28.000
They'd lost Apdo, their charismatic
solo-queue rebel leader, and without him

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.620
they kind of fell apart.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:33.480
In their second game against Samsung Ozone, Team Dark went full meme.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.460
(Casting)

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.320
They drafted an all-jungler composition
in honor of the then-recently-retired

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.460
Korean jungler CloudTemplar.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:47.000
(Casting)

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.440
Plus, Team Dark spelled out "Let's Go Gank"

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.000
if you read out the first
characters of their banned Champion's names.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:58.040
Team Dark's comp was never supposed to be
in a lane, so Samsung Ozone went just as memey.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.890
They drafted all AD carries and
bruisers, designed to push lanes and take

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.920
towers as fast as possible.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:11.700
(Casting)

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.100
They annihilated Team Dark in just over eight minutes.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:31.700
(Casting)

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:36.220
Three days later, KeSPA and OGN disqualified Team Dark for intentionally throwing

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:40.660
their matches. And as far as anyone knows, none of those players ever played

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.340
pro League of Legends ever again.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:46.980
Team Dark probably had it coming if you think about it.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:50.100
The highest level of League of
Legends competition in the world is

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:55.500
maybe not the best place for your
memorial meme comp. But Team Dark didn't care.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.730
They'd just lost Apdo, and while he'd
eventually return to solo queue, he's

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:03.680
still banned from playing under his own
name until the 31st century.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:09.660
His teammates' careers were forever
ruined, but they were also just solo queue randos.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:14.220
For his part, Apdo streams on
other accounts now, and says he'll pay

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.530
Riot $100,000 to get his main one back.
But Riot has every right to take apart

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:24.150
Elo boosters. These days Apdo mostly
streams from China, after winning a

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:28.410
contest that saw him take first place in
the solo queue rankings there and also

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.840
resulted in the single greatest picture
in esports history.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:38.100
But Apdo's competitive ban ended in 2015. There's no reason he couldn't try out for a pro

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:43.350
team right now, but Apdo doesn't care.
He doesn't want to play in Riot's system.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:47.280
Once upon a time he was the greatest midlaner in the world.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.580
But now, he's just a guy playing League
of Legends with a plate full of money.

